 # Diffusion-guided editing
 ## Overview
-Diffusion-guided editing modifies pre-trained NeRFs by leveraging 2D text-to-image diffusion models as external priors to guide 3D appearance and geometry changes [S1]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by either iteratively updating the training dataset with diffusion-edited views or directly backpropagating photometric losses from edited renders to update NeRF parameters, rather than relying solely on semantic masks or geometric constraints [14365-repaint-nerf.md, 15089-instruct-nerf2nerf-optimization.md].
